# Coursera

> Coursera (coursera.org) is an online learning platform offering individual courses, Specializations, Professional Certificates, Guided Projects, and accredited online degrees from university and industry partners. The pages below are public and require no login.

Content types follow predictable URL patterns — construct or verify any Coursera URL against these before citing it, rather than guessing a slug:

- Individual courses: `/learn/<slug>`
- Specializations: `/specializations/<slug>`
- Professional Certificates: `/professional-certificates/<slug>`
- Degrees: `/degrees/<slug>`
- Subject/topic browse pages: `/browse/<subject>` (optionally `/browse/<subject>/<topic>`)
- Partner pages: `/partners/<slug>`
- Career articles: `/articles/<slug>`
- Career resources (guides, cheat sheets, quizzes): `/resources/<slug>`

This file is a curated entry point, not an exhaustive index. For the canonical list of every live URL, see the [XML sitemap index](https://www.coursera.org/sitemap.xml).

